              "uncertainty": {
                "type": "object"
              },
              "provenance": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Where these numbers came from. 'measured_raster' / 'measured_vector' mean you READ them off a figure's marks; this check then REFUSES, because it tests whether a value is possible to its LAST PRINTED DIGIT and a measured value has no last printed digit. 'ocr_table' / 'ocr_text' mean a MACHINE transcribed the numeral off an image (any cell an extractor returned with provenance 'ocr_table' -- scanned supplements arrive this way); this check refuses those too, for a different reason: the digit exists but we may have misread it, and a misread digit yields `impossible` against arithmetic that was fine. Anything the paper printed and we read from a text layer -- table, text, or a numeral inside a figure -- is not measured and runs normally."
